Budget Analyst 
Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time
Worksite details: Onsite Full-Time/Redstone Arsenal, AL
Required Education and Experience 
BA/BS and 2 years or greater of experience in the field or related area
Or HS Diploma and 4 years or greater of specialized experience in the field or related area
Position Description 
Provide general accounting management support for funds control and distribution, payroll management, accounts receivables, funds balancing, cost management, property management, environment liabilities, procure to pay, grants execution and controls, reimbursable/non-reimbursable agreements, standard general ledger, appropriations integration, continuous monitoring program, and policy integration activities. This shall include, but is not limited to:
• Supporting the establishment of funds control over appropriated funds;
• Reviewing timecards on a bi-weekly basis for accuracy and make corrections of time and attendance data;
• Supporting processes related to other reimbursable and non-reimbursable agreements;
• Supporting Continuous Monitoring Program (CMP) reconciliations;
• Accounting and tracking of Space Act Agreements, International Agreements, General Services Administration (GSA) revenues, and other revenue receipts;
• Processing cost in NASA's accounting systems resulting in expenses and liabilities reflected in financial systems to include contract/account analysis and evaluation/resolution of issues;
• Supporting processes and procedures related to the accounting for and management of Government-held personal property, real property, operating materials and supplies, internal use of software and contractor-held property;
• Preparing Statements of Federal Financial Accounting Standards (SFFAS);
• Supporting the creation, approval, and review of purchase requests and the disbursement of those funds to vendors and contractors; (j) Financial monitoring of grants execution and controls;
• Ensuring general ledger accounts reconcile with Treasury accounts;
• Ensuring financial and grants policy and compliance; and
• Other reconciliations and monitoring of transactions/accounts
